JUCE 9.0.2 — Logic Pro AU sidechain bus-count bug fix

Root cause: JUCE's AU wrapper `JuceAU::SetBusCount()` syncs the stream-format
layout tag of the wrong bus when Logic adds a sidechain input bus
(kAudioUnitProperty_ElementCount input 1 -> 2). It updates element `busNr`
instead of the newly added element `busNr + 1`, so AudioUnitInitialize fails
with kAudioUnitErr_FormatNotSupported (-10868) and Logic falls back to the
generic view with no sound.

Apply this patch to a local JUCE source tree:

  /Users/abram/JUCE/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm

Reference: https://forum.juce.com/t/69501

--- a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm
@@ -347,7 +347,7 @@ OSStatus SetBusCount (AudioUnitScope scope, UInt32 count) override
                         if (! juceFilter->addBus (isInput))
                             break;

-                        err = syncAudioUnitWithChannelSet (isInput, busNr,
+                        err = syncAudioUnitWithChannelSet (isInput, busNr + 1,
                                                            juceFilter->getBus (isInput, busNr + 1)->getDefaultLayout());
                         if (err != noErr)
                             break;
